//? Title: YOLO v1 IoU responsibility and explicit prefix pretraining
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Check every YOLO v1 loss derivative and the actual full448-pixel convolution graph, show tensor affine data/crop examples, then visibly fit a crop classifier, transfer its prefix and fit every compact detector parameter with paired BN checkpoints.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/yolo_v1.cpp`.

> The method

YOLO v1 predicts two linear boxes and shared class scores per7x7 cell. Detached IoU responsibility chooses the coordinate predictor. Optional digit-crop pretraining initializes the first20 convolutions, followed by explicit whole-detector optimization.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/yolo_v1_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/yolo_v1_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/yolo_v1_concept.tikz > build/yolo_v1_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/yolo_v1_concept.svg build/yolo_v1_concept.dvi > build/yolo_v1_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
