> Paper convolution graph and bounded dense-head accounting

The full448-pixel RGB architecture has24 convolutions with leaky-ReLU slope.1,
no BN and a7x7x1024 final map. The following actually differentiates all48
convolution kernel/bias tensors. Its60,155,968 convolution scalars plus a
211,547,582-scalar4096-wide dense head give271,703,550 total. The huge dense
head is counted from shapes rather than allocated; the full detector is not
claimed to have been trained. Compact fitting below executes both dense layers.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  n::ParameterStore p(17);
  const auto net = n::models::YoloV1Backbone(
      p, nullptr, n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 448 * 448 * 3)).reshape({1, 448, 448, 3}));
  if (net.features.shape() != n::Shape{1, 7, 7, 1024} || net.convolutions.size() != 24 ||
      p.count() != 60155968)
    return 1;
  const auto g = n::grad(n::mean(n::square(net.features)), p.parameters());
  if (g.size() != 48)
    return 1;
  for (const auto &v : g)
    if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v)).item()))
      return 1;
  const std::int64_t head = std::int64_t(7 * 7 * 1024) * 4096 + 4096 + 4096 * 1470 + 1470;
  if (p.count() + head != 271703550)
    return 1;
  std::print("Executed full448RGB backbone:{} convolution scalars,{} finite defined "
             "gradients,7x7x1024 features. Dense head counted from shapes:{} scalars; "
             "total{}. Full huge head is not allocated/fitted.\n",
             p.count(), g.size(), head, p.count() + head);
}
```
