> Actual56-pixel data and tensor affine/exposure augmentation

The compact model retains all24 convolutions, with widths divided by eight,
256 dense units and7x7x128 features at56gray pixels. It removes the original
first/22nd strides and fourth pooling operation. This report enables the
source's optional BN experiment (momentum.9,epsilon1e-5), disables dropout,
and has2,801,020 learned/3,296 moving-state scalars. Without BN the same model
has2,799,372 learned scalars and no moving state. These differ from the paper's
unnormalized full model.

Scenes use64 fit/16 validation examples from the first2048 MNIST training
digits,seed11, and eight test scenes from the first512 official test digits,
seed22, generated directly on56x56 canvases. They are not the64-pixel scene
layout used by previous reports. The gallery compares actual inputs with
explicit scale/translation/exposure variants. Inverse pixel-centre bilinear
sampling and boxes use matching transforms, with zero image padding and
clipped boxes. Pixel quantization is tensor half-up rounding to bytes/255.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/yolo_v1_scenes.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto train = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  n::models::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
  cfg.scenes = 80;
  cfg.height = cfg.width = 56;
  cfg.seed = 11;
  const auto scenes = n::models::MakeTensorDetectionScenes(
      n::slice_axis(train.images, 0, 0, 2048), n::slice_axis(train.labels, 0, 0, 2048), cfg);

  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows = {0, 1, 2, 3};
  const auto augmented = n::models::TransformTensorDetectionScenes(
      scenes, rows,
      n::tensor({1., 0., 0., 1., 1., .5, .5, 1., 1.2, -3., 2., 1.3, .8, 2., -3., .8}, {4, 4}));
  std::vector<n::Tensor> boxes(scenes.boxes.begin(), scenes.boxes.begin() + 4);
  const auto before = n::models::DrawDetectionBoxes(n::slice_axis(scenes.images, 0, 0, 4),
                                                    boxes, {.1, 1., .2});
  const auto after =
      n::models::DrawDetectionBoxes(augmented.images, augmented.boxes, {.1, 1., .2});
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat({before, after}, 0), "build/yolo_v1_scenes.png", 4, 0., 1., 4,
                     1., 2);
  std::int64_t objects = 0;
  for (const auto &b : scenes.boxes)
    objects += b.shape()[0];
  std::print(
      "80 generated training/validation scenes; {} accepted digits. Preview: first "
      "four training scenes above, corresponding tensor affine/exposure variants below.\n",
      objects);
}
```
