> Conclusion

The prefix classifier selects epoch8 at validation NLL1.453287 and accuracy.488889 on45 crops (168 fitting crops,88 Adam steps). Some crops contain neighbouring overlapping digits, making classification ambiguous. The detector selects its last epoch, 12, at validation AP50 .006528, which is still rising when the short run stops; test AP50/AP75/AP50:95 are .029141/0/.014282 with 748 detections. The training loss falls tenfold, from 25.79 to 2.52. Localization/generalization remain limited despite lower training loss.

The report separates full448-pixel backbone validation and analytic huge-head accounting from actual compact dense-head fitting. Prefix and detector optimizers, objectives, checkpoint selection and state transfer are explicit, with actual input/crop/test galleries and measured held-out results.

> References

- [Redmon et al. (2016), You Only Look Once: Unified, Real-Time Object Detection](https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.02640).
- [Authors’ Darknet project](https://github.com/pjreddie/darknet).
